# Phase 3 CLI acceptance — word-family / lemma inspection surface (SC3, G-02, D-10).
#
# Segment 2 of 2 (host-backed, D-13): the segment-1 import has reached its
# host-owned terminal state. The family/lemma commands are top-level (D-10's
# `qai quran family <kind> <id>` / `qai quran lemma <lemma>`), and with no
# active morphology dataset both are typed-unavailable — never an empty list.

```console
$ qai quran activate test-edition-min@0.1.0 --yes
activated test-edition-min@0.1.0 (generation 1)

```

```console
$ qai quran forms rebuild test-edition-min@0.1.0
rebuilt forms for quran-edition:test-edition-min@0.1.0: 14 ayahs, 64 tokens, 18 skeletons (generation 1)
MV-018 canonical-unchanged: pass (sha256:235795cb218c2df44496265b4ba5c3377d48944cb28cc4ff64c6104770932704)
provenance: prov-forms-test-edition-min-0.1.0-g1-[..]

```

The family surface is a first-class command (not nested under `morphology`):
it parses and reaches its handler, and it is typed-unavailable without an
active lexicon (QAI-MORPH-0004), never a 200-style empty relation list.

```console
$ qai quran family token token:1:1:1
? 5
error: no active morphology dataset for word family; import and activate one first

```

An empty kind or id is a usage error before any database read.

```console
$ qai quran family "" token:1:1:1
? 2
error: family needs a non-empty <kind> and <id>

```

The D-10 top-level `lemma` alias reaches the lemma read path and is
typed-unavailable without an active lexicon.

```console
$ qai quran lemma كتب
? 5
error: no active morphology dataset for lemma search; import and activate one first

```
